WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
December 2024.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:07.170
A new malaria vaccine, R21,
reaches two Nigerian states:

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.430
Kebbi in the north, Bayelsa in the south.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.050
1 million doses, in the country with
the largest share of malaria deaths.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:21.770
In 2024, malaria killed an
estimated 610,000 people.

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.990
95 per cent of them died
in the WHO African Region.

7
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.350
Why there?

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.790
And why do young children die most?

9
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.410
Do the mosquitoes live only in Africa?

10
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.050
In this mission, you'll
follow Plasmodium parasites,

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.130
and the Anopheles
mosquitoes that carry them.

12
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.810
Then you'll weigh physical
and human factors,

13
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.630
track an invading mosquito,
and judge the responses.

14
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.730
Your mission: explain why malaria
kills mostly in one continent,

15
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.760
and mostly young children.
